1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,480
No will? Your state already wrote yours.

2
00:00:02,500 --> 00:00:04,380
You've probably never read it.

3
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:07,747
It ranks who gets your stuff. Yes, that sibling too.

4
00:00:07,767 --> 00:00:11,147
Not married? Your partner usually gets nothing.

5
00:00:11,167 --> 00:00:14,347
Kids? If no parent is left, a judge decides.

6
00:00:14,367 --> 00:00:17,113
Usually a relative. Maybe not your pick.

7
00:00:17,133 --> 00:00:20,113
You can replace it. A will is where you decide.

8
00:00:20,133 --> 00:00:23,280
Who gets what. Who you'd name for kids. Who's in charge.

9
00:00:23,300 --> 00:00:26,513
Unsigned? The state's version is still yours.

10
00:00:26,533 --> 00:00:29,147
Send this to the person you'd actually pick.

11
00:00:29,167 --> 00:00:34,547
Follow for the rules nobody reads, in plain English.
[On screen] Plainwill is not a law firm and is not a substitute for the advice of an attorney.

